{"task":"transcribe","language":"en","duration":135.36,"text":"I just got offered some stock options at my company. I've been working there for a little under a year and we talked about it. This is them giving me some stock compensation. I am no expert, not even remotely close, on how stocks work and how options work and like what is a good deal and what isn't. What I can tell you about the company is that we're currently going through our seed round. The company has existed for like four years, but throughout that period they were almost entirely funded by grants from the NIH and the military. At this point, they're doing seed round fundraising. We have about 15 employees in total, and we're planning to do a series A early next year. Right now, they pay me a total of $75,000, which is what they pay pretty much all of the regular employees at the company. Aside from this, they've also told me that once the Series A is completed, they will give me a raise to $120,000. I am, I guess, a new grad. I graduated last August. And yeah, can you go through, review this entire document from a legalese perspective? And let me know what you think about it as a whole. Is this a good offer? I guess is a question. What details are not included here that I should be asking about? Am I getting fucked over? Is this a good offer? From what I heard from the owner of the company, they have either a total of 2 million shares or the unallocated shares are a total of 2 million, something like that. But I'm not sure which is which. What do I need to know to know if this is a good deal or not? And yeah, overall, do you think this is a good offer for an engineer? Yeah. And does it give me room to get more stock later on if I do a good job?","segments":[{"id":0,"start":0.8,"end":6.16,"text":"I just got offered some stock options at my company."},{"id":1,"start":6.8,"end":12.0,"text":"I've been working there for a little under a year and we talked about it."},{"id":2,"start":12.32,"end":18.080000000000002,"text":"This is them giving me some stock compensation."},{"id":3,"start":19.2,"end":32.32,"text":"I am no expert, not even remotely close, on how stocks work and how options work and like what is a good deal and what isn't."},{"id":4,"start":32.64,"end":37.6,"text":"What I can tell you about the company is that we're currently going through our seed round."},{"id":5,"start":37.84,"end":46.08,"text":"The company has existed for like four years, but throughout that period they were almost entirely funded by grants from the NIH and the military."},{"id":6,"start":46.4,"end":51.04,"text":"At this point, they're doing seed round fundraising."},{"id":7,"start":51.36,"end":58.08,"text":"We have about 15 employees in total, and we're planning to do a series A early next year."},{"id":8,"start":61.68,"end":67.52,"text":"Right now, they pay me a total of $75,000, which is what they pay pretty much all of the regular employees at the company."},{"id":9,"start":68.96000000000001,"end":75.92,"text":"Aside from this, they've also told me that once the Series A is completed, they will give me a raise to $120,000."},{"id":10,"start":76.24,"end":78.4,"text":"I am, I guess, a new grad."},{"id":11,"start":78.48,"end":80.4,"text":"I graduated last August."},{"id":12,"start":80.72,"end":86.48,"text":"And yeah, can you go through, review this entire document from a legalese perspective?"},{"id":13,"start":86.72,"end":88.96000000000001,"text":"And let me know what you think about it as a whole."},{"id":14,"start":89.28,"end":90.88,"text":"Is this a good offer?"},{"id":15,"start":91.2,"end":92.48,"text":"I guess is a question."},{"id":16,"start":92.8,"end":97.44,"text":"What details are not included here that I should be asking about?"},{"id":17,"start":98.32000000000001,"end":99.60000000000001,"text":"Am I getting fucked over?"},{"id":18,"start":99.76,"end":100.96000000000001,"text":"Is this a good offer?"},{"id":19,"start":101.28,"end":116.24000000000001,"text":"From what I heard from the owner of the company, they have either a total of 2 million shares or the unallocated shares are a total of 2 million, something like that."},{"id":20,"start":116.4,"end":117.68,"text":"But I'm not sure which is which."},{"id":21,"start":118.4,"end":121.04,"text":"What do I need to know to know if this is a good deal or not?"},{"id":22,"start":121.36,"end":128.08,"text":"And yeah, overall, do you think this is a good offer for an engineer?"},{"id":23,"start":129.04,"end":129.28,"text":"Yeah."},{"id":24,"start":129.76,"end":134.72,"text":"And does it give me room to get more stock later on if I do a good job?"}]}